@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-interpretation-time`

-- Tests of usca-interpretation-time.l4, second file: the rules that are not period counting.  Each expected value is decided
-- from the section cited above the assertion, never from the module.  A failing assertion is a finding.

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sundays only` d MEANS `is a Sunday` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays and Sundays` d MEANS `is a Saturday` d OR `is a Sunday` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every day is a holiday` d MEANS TRUE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no day is a business day` d MEANS FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` d MEANS `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 4 3

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` d MEANS
    `Weekday of` d AT LEAST 1 AND `Weekday of` d AT MOST 5 AND NOT `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` d MEANS NOT `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Moment
`a moment on` d `at second` s MEANS Moment WITH `the day` IS d, `seconds after midnight` IS s

GIVEN session IS A `Session of enactment`
      d IS A DATE
      adjourned IS A MAYBE DATE
      election IS A BOOLEAN
      tax IS A BOOLEAN
      appropriations IS A BOOLEAN
      urgency IS A BOOLEAN
      own IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`test enactment` session d adjourned election tax appropriations urgency own MEANS
    `Enactment of a statute` WITH
        `the session` IS session
        `the moment of enactment` IS `a moment on` d `at second` 36000
        `the special session adjourned on` IS adjourned
        `calls an election` IS election
        `provides for a tax levy` IS tax
        `provides for appropriations for the usual current expenses of the state` IS appropriations
        `is an urgency statute` IS urgency
        `names its own day of effect` IS own

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`a regular-session statute enacted on` d MEANS
    `test enactment` `a regular session` d NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`an election statute enacted on` d MEANS
    `test enactment` `a regular session` d NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`a tax levy statute enacted on` d MEANS
    `test enactment` `a regular session` d NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`a usual-expenses appropriation statute enacted on` d MEANS
    `test enactment` `a regular session` d NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`an urgency statute enacted on` d MEANS
    `test enactment` `a regular session` d NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      adjourned IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`a special-session statute enacted on` d `after the special session adjourned on` adjourned MEANS
    `test enactment` `a special session` d (JUST adjourned) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`a special-session statute with no adjournment date given, enacted on` d MEANS
    `test enactment` `a special session` d NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      named IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Enactment of a statute`
`a regular-session statute enacted on` d `that names its own day` named MEANS
    `test enactment` `a regular session` d NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST named)


§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 12c: counting backward from a hearing date`

-- § 12c(a): count backward from the hearing date, excluding the day of the hearing; (b): added days for a method of service are counted
-- backward from the day (a) gives.  So the last day is the hearing date less n less the added days.
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 9 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 1 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 9)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 9 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 2 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 30)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 14 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 5 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Saturdays and Sundays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 22)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 14 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 5 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 22)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 2 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Saturdays and Sundays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 8)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 30 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 11)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 8 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 2)
-- Crossing a 29 February: hearing Friday 1 March 2024, two days before is Wednesday 28 February, one day before Thursday 29 February.
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 2 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2024 3 1) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 28)
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 1 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2024 3 1) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 29)
-- Crossing a year end: hearing Monday 5 January 2026, five days before is Wednesday 31 December 2025.
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 5 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 1 5) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2025 12 31)
-- The 12c days before and the method-of-service days are added, in either order: 14 and 5 equal 19 and 0 and 5 and 14.
#ASSERT `the last day to act, when the act is due` 19 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 22)
-- A last day on a holiday: § 12a(a) moves a last day forward, § 12 excludes it, and neither says which way a backward count moves.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day to act, when the act is due` 10 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 12c counts backward from the hearing date, and § 12a(a) moves a last day that is a holiday forward, to the next day that is not a holiday, while § 12 excludes it; the text does not say which way a backward-counted last day moves when it falls on a holiday"
-- Not a whole number of days, or no days, or negative added days: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day to act, when the act is due` 0 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(a) speaks of a specified number of days before a hearing date; the text does not count part of a day or no days"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day to act, when the act is due` -3 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(a) speaks of a specified number of days before a hearing date; the text does not count part of a day or no days"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day to act, when the act is due` 1.5 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(a) speaks of a specified number of days before a hearing date; the text does not count part of a day or no days"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day to act, when the act is due` 5 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` -1 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(b) speaks of additional days added because of a method of service; the text does not count part of a day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day to act, when the act is due` 5 `days before the hearing on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 1.5 `added days for the method of service, under the calendar` `Sundays only` BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(b) speaks of additional days added because of a method of service; the text does not count part of a day"

§ `Gov. Code § 6706, Civ. Code § 11, Code Civ. Proc. § 13: an act appointed for a particular day`

-- The act appointed for a particular day that falls on a holiday may be performed 'upon the next business day with the same effect'.
-- Two readings of 'business day' are supplied: Monday to Friday outside the holidays (usual), and every day that is not a holiday (Civ. Code § 9).
-- Holidays here: Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026.
-- Friday 3 April 2026 is a holiday here.  Next business day: Monday 6 April on the weekday reading, Saturday 4 April on the Civ. Code § 9 reading.
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 3) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 3) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 4)
-- Sunday 5 April 2026 is a holiday: Monday 6 April on either reading.
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 5) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 5) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
-- A day that is not a holiday: no change.  Thursday 2 April, Saturday 4 April, Monday 6 April.
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 2) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 2)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 2) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 2)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 4) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 4)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 4) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 4)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 6) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 6) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
-- An act that is not secular, or is a work of necessity or mercy: the rule gives it no later day.
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 3) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` FALSE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 3)
#ASSERT `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 5) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` FALSE `and given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 5)
-- A calendar with no business day within 366 days is refused rather than looped over.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the latest day on which an act appointed for` (YMD 2026 4 5) `may be performed with the same effect, given that it is secular:` TRUE `and given the holidays` `every day is a holiday` `and the business days` `no day is a business day` BECAUSE "the calendar supplied makes more than 366 consecutive days not business days, so there is no next business day"
-- The next business day after a date, directly.
#ASSERT `the next business day after` (YMD 2026 4 2) `under the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the next business day after` (YMD 2026 4 2) `under the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 4)
#ASSERT `the next business day after` (YMD 2026 4 6) `under the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 7)
#ASSERT `the next business day after` (YMD 2026 4 3) `under the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the next business day after` (YMD 2026 4 2) `under the business days` `no day is a business day` BECAUSE "the calendar supplied makes more than 366 consecutive days not business days, so there is no next business day"

§ `Gov. Code § 6707: the last day for filing with a state agency`

-- § 6707: when the last day 'falls upon a Saturday or holiday', the act may be performed upon the next business day.
-- Saturday 4 April: next business day Monday 6 April on either reading (Sunday is a holiday, so not a business day on either).
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 4) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 4) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
-- Friday 3 April (a holiday here): Monday on the weekday reading, Saturday on the Civ. Code § 9 reading.
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 3) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 3) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 4)
-- Sunday 5 April (a holiday): Monday 6 April.
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 5) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 5) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
-- Saturday 11 April, on a calendar where Saturday is not a holiday, is still moved: § 6707 names Saturday itself.
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 11) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 13)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 11) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 13)
-- A day that is neither: unchanged.  Monday 6 April, Wednesday 8 April, Friday 10 April.
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 6) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 6) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 6)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 8) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 8)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 8) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 8)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 10) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `business days from Monday to Friday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 10)
#ASSERT `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 10) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `every day that is not a holiday, outside Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 10)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the latest day for filing with a state agency, when the last day is` (YMD 2026 4 4) `, given the holidays` `Sundays and Friday 3 April 2026` `and the business days` `no day is a business day` BECAUSE "the calendar supplied makes more than 366 consecutive days not business days, so there is no next business day"

§ `Code Civ. Proc. §§ 13a, 13b: acts that may be performed on a Saturday or a special holiday`

#ASSERT `an act required by law on a day or within a period may be performed on` `a Saturday`
#ASSERT `an act required by law on a day or within a period may be performed on` `a special holiday`
#ASSERT REFUSED `an act required by law on a day or within a period may be performed on` `a Sunday or another holiday that is not a special holiday` BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. §§ 13a and 13b say an act may be performed on a special holiday or on a Saturday; the text does not say whether an act may be performed on a Sunday or on another holiday (§ 13 and Civ. Code § 11 give the next business day for an act appointed for a particular day, which is a different question)"

§ `Gov. Code § 9600(a): a statute enacted at a regular session`

-- § 9600(a): 'January 1 next following a 90-day period from the date of enactment'.  Read with § 6800: the day of enactment is excluded,
-- so the 90-day period ends on the 90th day after it.  Fork F-commence in NOTES: when that 90th day is itself a January 1, 'next following' is refused.
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2025 12 31)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 2) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 2)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 3) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9600(a) says January 1 next following a 90-day period from the date of enactment; when the 90th day is itself a January 1 the text does not say whether that day is part of the period (so the next January 1 follows it) or the period ends the day before (so that January 1 is the next following)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 3)) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9600(a) says January 1 next following a 90-day period from the date of enactment; when the 90th day is itself a January 1 the text does not say whether that day is part of the period (so the next January 1 follows it) or the period ends the day before (so that January 1 is the next following)"
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 4) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 4)) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 5) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 10 5)) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 12 31)) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2027 1 1)) EQUALS (YMD 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 7 4) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 7 4)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 4 1)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 4 2) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 4 2)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2026 4 3) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 4 3)) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a regular-session statute goes into effect when enacted on` (YMD 2025 10 3) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9600(a) says January 1 next following a 90-day period from the date of enactment; when the 90th day is itself a January 1 the text does not say whether that day is part of the period (so the next January 1 follows it) or the period ends the day before (so that January 1 is the next following)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2025 10 3)) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9600(a) says January 1 next following a 90-day period from the date of enactment; when the 90th day is itself a January 1 the text does not say whether that day is part of the period (so the next January 1 follows it) or the period ends the day before (so that January 1 is the next following)"
