§ `The moment a statute enacted under § 9600(a) binds`

-- § 9600(a) names a day.  The deposited text names no moment of it: § 6806 says a day is from midnight to midnight, and Civ. Code § 2 and Code Civ. Proc. § 2 fix noon for those codes alone.  Refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment a statute goes into effect` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9600(a) names the day a statute goes into effect and no moment of it; § 6806 says only that a day runs from one midnight to the next, and Civ. Code § 2 and Code Civ. Proc. § 2 (noon) speak of those codes alone"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment a statute goes into effect` (`a special-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `after the special session adjourned on` (YMD 2026 3 5)) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9600(a) names the day a statute goes into effect and no moment of it; § 6806 says only that a day runs from one midnight to the next, and Civ. Code § 2 and Code Civ. Proc. § 2 (noon) speak of those codes alone"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the statute binds at the moment` (`a moment on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `at second` 0) `given its enactment` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9600(a) names the day a statute goes into effect and no moment of it; § 6806 says only that a day runs from one midnight to the next, and Civ. Code § 2 and Code Civ. Proc. § 2 (noon) speak of those codes alone"
-- A caller who reads the day to begin at midnight can say so, and then the answer is the midnight that begins the day.
#ASSERT (`the moment a statute goes into effect, taking it to bind from the midnight that begins its day` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10)))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT (`the moment a statute goes into effect, taking it to bind from the midnight that begins its day` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10)))'s `seconds after midnight` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the moment a statute goes into effect, taking it to bind from the midnight that begins its day` (`a special-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `after the special session adjourned on` (YMD 2026 2 5)))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 7)
#ASSERT (`the moment a statute goes into effect, taking it to bind from the midnight that begins its day` (`an urgency statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10)))'s `seconds after midnight` EQUALS 36000
-- Under that reading: a moment before the midnight is not bound, the midnight and later are.
#ASSERT `the moment` (`a moment on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `at second` 0) `is not before the moment` (`the moment a statute goes into effect, taking it to bind from the midnight that begins its day` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10)))
#ASSERT NOT (`the moment` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 12 31) `at second` 86399) `is not before the moment` (`the moment a statute goes into effect, taking it to bind from the midnight that begins its day` (`a regular-session statute enacted on` (YMD 2026 3 10))))

