-- The day daylight saving time commences, 8 March 2026: before 2 a.m. standard, 3 a.m. onward daylight, 2 to 3 a.m. does not occur.
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 0))
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 7199))
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 10800)
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 86399)
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 7200) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time commences at 2 a.m., when the clock advances one hour, so the clock does not read between 2 a.m. and 3 a.m. that day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 9000) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time commences at 2 a.m., when the clock advances one hour, so the clock does not read between 2 a.m. and 3 a.m. that day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 10799) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time commences at 2 a.m., when the clock advances one hour, so the clock does not read between 2 a.m. and 3 a.m. that day"
-- The day it ends, 1 November 2026: before 1 a.m. daylight, 2 a.m. onward standard, 1 to 2 a.m. occurs twice and is refused.
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 0)
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 3599)
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 7200))
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 86399))
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 3600) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time ends at 2 a.m., so the clock reads between 1 a.m. and 2 a.m. twice that day; the text does not say which of the two a bare reading means, nor whether 2 a.m. there is read on the daylight clock or the standard one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 5000) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time ends at 2 a.m., so the clock reads between 1 a.m. and 2 a.m. twice that day; the text does not say which of the two a bare reading means, nor whether 2 a.m. there is read on the daylight clock or the standard one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 7199) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time ends at 2 a.m., so the clock reads between 1 a.m. and 2 a.m. twice that day; the text does not say which of the two a bare reading means, nor whether 2 a.m. there is read on the daylight clock or the standard one"
-- Hours the clock is advanced from standard time.
#ASSERT `hours the clock is advanced from standard time at` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `at second` 43200) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `hours the clock is advanced from standard time at` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `at second` 43200) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `hours the clock is advanced from standard time at` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 10800) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `hours the clock is advanced from standard time at` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 3600) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `hours the clock is advanced from standard time at` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 7200) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `hours the clock is advanced from standard time at` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `at second` 7200) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time commences at 2 a.m., when the clock advances one hour, so the clock does not read between 2 a.m. and 3 a.m. that day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `hours the clock is advanced from standard time at` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `at second` 3600) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time ends at 2 a.m., so the clock reads between 1 a.m. and 2 a.m. twice that day; the text does not say which of the two a bare reading means, nor whether 2 a.m. there is read on the daylight clock or the standard one"
-- Another year: second Sunday of March 2027 is 14 March, first Sunday of November 2027 is 7 November.
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2027 3 13) `at second` 86399))
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2027 3 14) `at second` 10800)
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2027 11 6) `at second` 86399)
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2027 11 7) `at second` 7200))
-- The pre-2026 days the old rule might have given are not special here: 2026-03-08 is the second Sunday, 2026-03-15 is not a boundary.
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `at second` 7200)
#ASSERT `daylight saving time is in effect at the clock reading` (`a moment on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `at second` 3600)

§ `Which section governs, by kind of enactment`

-- The three definitions of 'month' say the same thing, so each code's own definition governs its own provisions, and § 6804 the Government Code and other statutes.
#ASSERT `the section that defines month for` `a provision of the Civil Code` EQUALS "Civ. Code § 14(b)(4)"
#ASSERT `the section that defines month for` `a provision of the Code of Civil Procedure` EQUALS "Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(4)"
#ASSERT `the section that defines month for` `a provision of the Government Code` EQUALS "Gov. Code § 6804"
#ASSERT `the section that defines month for` `a provision of another State statute` EQUALS "Gov. Code § 6804"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section that defines month for` `an ordinance, rule or regulation` BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6804 does not say whether it reaches an ordinance, rule or regulation; the text names those only in Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(b), which concerns the last day of a period"
#ASSERT `the section that extends a last day falling on a holiday for` `a provision of the Civil Code` EQUALS "Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), by § 12a(b); Civ. Code § 10 also excludes the day"
#ASSERT `the section that extends a last day falling on a holiday for` `a provision of the Code of Civil Procedure` EQUALS "Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a); § 12 also excludes the day"
#ASSERT `the section that extends a last day falling on a holiday for` `a provision of the Government Code` EQUALS "Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), by § 12a(b); Gov. Code § 6800 also excludes the day"
#ASSERT `the section that extends a last day falling on a holiday for` `a provision of another State statute` EQUALS "Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), by § 12a(b); Gov. Code § 6800 also excludes the day"
#ASSERT `the section that extends a last day falling on a holiday for` `an ordinance, rule or regulation` EQUALS "Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), by § 12a(b)"
#ASSERT `the section that says which days are holidays for` `a provision of the Civil Code` EQUALS "Civ. Code § 7"
#ASSERT `the section that says which days are holidays for` `a provision of the Code of Civil Procedure` EQUALS "Code Civ. Proc. § 10"
#ASSERT `the section that says which days are holidays for` `a provision of the Government Code` EQUALS "Gov. Code § 6700(a)"
#ASSERT `the section that says which days are holidays for` `a provision of another State statute` EQUALS "Gov. Code § 6700(a)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section that says which days are holidays for` `an ordinance, rule or regulation` BECAUSE "no deposited section says which holiday list governs an ordinance, rule or regulation; Gov. Code § 6700(a) says only 'the holidays in this state', and Gov. Code §§ 6700(a)(20)(B), 6702 and 6704 give cities, counties and districts their own rules for some days"

§ `The business-day loop guard`

-- 366 days in a row that are not business days still resolve; 367 are refused.  This is a limit on the calendar supplied, not a rule of the text.

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`business days only from 4 April 2027` d MEANS d AT LEAST (YMD 2027 4 4)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`business days only from 5 April 2027` d MEANS d AT LEAST (YMD 2027 4 5)

#ASSERT `the next business day after` (YMD 2026 4 2) `under the business days` `business days only from 4 April 2027` EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 4)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the next business day after` (YMD 2026 4 2) `under the business days` `business days only from 5 April 2027` BECAUSE "the calendar supplied makes more than 366 consecutive days not business days, so there is no next business day"
#ASSERT `next business day after the date, counting days so far` `business days only from 4 April 2027` (YMD 2026 4 2) 0 EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 4)
#ASSERT `next business day after the date, counting days so far` `business days only from 4 April 2027` (YMD 2027 4 3) 365 EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 4)
#ASSERT REFUSED `next business day after the date, counting days so far` `business days only from 5 April 2027` (YMD 2026 4 2) 366 BECAUSE "the calendar supplied makes more than 366 consecutive days not business days, so there is no next business day"
#ASSERT `next business day after the date, counting days so far` `business days only from 5 April 2027` (YMD 2027 4 4) 366 EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 5)
-- Daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it commences or ends, directly (seconds after midnight).
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it commences` 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it commences` 7199)
#ASSERT `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it commences` 10800
#ASSERT `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it commences` 86399
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it commences` 7200 BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time commences at 2 a.m., when the clock advances one hour, so the clock does not read between 2 a.m. and 3 a.m. that day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it commences` 10799 BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time commences at 2 a.m., when the clock advances one hour, so the clock does not read between 2 a.m. and 3 a.m. that day"
#ASSERT `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it ends` 0
#ASSERT `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it ends` 3599
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it ends` 7200)
#ASSERT NOT (`daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it ends` 86399)
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it ends` 3600 BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time ends at 2 a.m., so the clock reads between 1 a.m. and 2 a.m. twice that day; the text does not say which of the two a bare reading means, nor whether 2 a.m. there is read on the daylight clock or the standard one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `daylight saving time at a clock reading on the day it ends` 7199 BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(b): daylight saving time ends at 2 a.m., so the clock reads between 1 a.m. and 2 a.m. twice that day; the text does not say which of the two a bare reading means, nor whether 2 a.m. there is read on the daylight clock or the standard one"
